        {
          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"contract_version\":\"compact-1.1.0\",\"paper_id\":\"GP-009\",\"eligibility\":{\"decision\":\"ineligible\",\"reason_codes\":[\"ORIGINAL_EXPERIMENT\",\"IDENTIFIABLE_LNP\",\"SUPPORTED_PAYLOAD\",\"USABLE_FORMULATION_OUTCOME_LINKAGE\",\"NO_TARGET_CELL_EVIDENCE\"],\"evidence_ids\":[\"GP-009-E-52aa2dcb19fee404\",\"GP-009-E-9f8f06cd49f73aa6\",\"GP-009-E-6e3f276531062d8c\",\"GP-009-E-eebd6e63463b8d5b\"],\"explanation\":\"The packet reports original in vivo and in vitro mRNA-LNP experiments with linked formulations and outcomes, but it does not report delivery to hepatocytes, Kupffer cells, LSECs, or hepatic stellate cells. Reported liver-level uptake/expression cannot be treated as evidence for a qualifying hepatic target cell.\"},\"formulations\":[],\"components\":[],\"experiments\":[],\"outcomes\":[],\"unresolved_items\":[\"Liver-level biodistribution and luciferase-expression results do not identify the liver cell type receiving LNP-mRNA.\",\"RAW 264.7 macrophages are reported, but the packet does not identify them as Kupffer cells.\"]}",
